      "text": "So I was at the grocery store the other day, and of course, I picked the slowest line. I don't know how it always happens. Every time I think I've chosen the shortest one, it somehow turns into a full-on traffic jam. There were, like, five people ahead of me, but the first woman was paying in coins, actual coins. She was counting them one by one, and I could feel my soul slowly leaving my body. I tried to play it cool, pulled out my phone, pretended to check messages, even though I had no signal, ",
